<GuideLayout 
  title="4-Needle 6-Thread Flatlock: The Engineering Behind High-Stress Athletic Seams" 
  type="CRAFTSMANSHIP"
  description="Technical analysis of high-performance stitching. Why professional activewear brands choose flatlock over standard seams."
>
  <h2>The Backbone of Athletic Apparel</h2>
  <p>In high-intensity training, the seam is the most common point of failure. Fitclo's <strong>4-Needle 6-Thread (4N6T)</strong> flatlock stitching is the industry standard for durability and skin comfort.</p>
  
  <h3>Stitch Density & Pull Strength</h3>
  <p>Standard overlock seams create a "bulge" that can chafe the skin and snap under tension. Our 4N6T machines create a flat, interlocking seam that is as strong as the fabric itself. In our internal pull tests, our flatlock seams withstand up to 45 lbs of direct tension before failure.</p>
  
  <h3>Anti-Chafe Engineering</h3>
  <p>By eliminating the seam allowance and creating a perfectly flat surface, we prevent friction against the skin during repetitive movements like running or squatting. This is a critical quality marker for premium brands aiming for the $100+ price point.</p>

  <h3>Inventory Management of Specialized Machinery</h3>
  <p>Maintaining a fleet of 200+ specialized flatlock machines requires dedicated <strong>Inventory Management</strong> for precision needles and high-tensile threads. As your <strong>Supply Chain Partner</strong>, we ensure our machinery is always calibrated for peak performance.</p>
</GuideLayout>
